 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? Find a dry spot in the circle, preferably near the center. Then clear a circle around the fire of loose wood and rocks. Yes, they roll away. Make the outer edge of the fire of rocks so it' easy to find. Yes, very useful. Pack them out of the fire first, though. It should never touch the dam, or the fire will go out. Use a separate fire for the fire sticks, in the middle and away from the main fire. Push it down so only the top of the stick is in the damper, then roll heavy rocks on top. It' be cold the next morning.",
